From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: TerminalApp: OpenBook's pinned image, verified
 before it is installed

On a build that isn't debuggable, the Terminal app downloaded Google's
image, which has no quired for Quire's agents. Its install also wrote
each tar entry to dir.resolve(name) as the archive streamed in, with no
check on the name, and marked the install complete only at the end.

The image now comes from OpenBook's manifest,
/product/etc/openbook/linux-env.json (URL, SHA-256, size, installed
size), on every build type. A debuggable build still takes
/sdcard/linux/images.tar.gz first, for the checks. A manifest with no
URL, an invalid one, or an OpenBook build whose manifest is missing
reports no_image and downloads nothing: never Google's. A build without
OpenBook's folder keeps AOSP's download.

OpenBook's image is installed in four steps (openbook/):
- staged in no-backup storage (linux-staging/images.tar.gz.part with
  staging.json), and continued after a restart with a Range request,
  sent with If-Range and kept only on a 206 whose Content-Range starts
  where the file ends; a 200, another range or a changed manifest
  starts over;
- verified whole, size and SHA-256, before anything is extracted;
- extracted into <install>.new, refusing absolute paths, "..", paths
  outside the folder or in a subfolder, links, devices, FIFOs, folders,
  names AOSP's installer doesn't know, a name twice, and more than the
  installed size;
- swapped in by rename after the marker is written. What the person
  has in the folder that isn't part of an image (root_part_backup) is
  kept; a crash mid-swap is finished or undone on the next install.
A refused image is dropped and not retried. A free-space check comes
first. AOSP's streamed install, still used for /sdcard and Google's
image, refuses entries that would leave the folder.

The agent bridge reports no_image, the install's phase (download,
verify, unpack), bytes and total, gets call("stop"), and offers vsock
port 7691, quired's root worker in the guest, beside 7690.

OpenBook ANAL-393 (Quire setup).

